    {
      "id": "claim_509f9f03b3c24d9fb0c5ec8208c6691d",
      "statement": "Gateway MCP tools are loaded fresh per invocation because the AgentCore Gateway OAuth token is short-lived; `load_gateway_tools()` mints a client-credentials token, builds a `MultiServerMCPClient` for `AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_URL`, and returns tools that are then threaded through runtime context rather than cached at module load.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://fionaa/app/fionaa/gateway.py#L27-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5dbcaf0a87f0e3915d59002d712a896223aa6b707c011471cb810f0924e423b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://fionaa/app/fionaa/main.py#L33-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4538abea4b1454ff3be59dec1e8cebcc84adaa2cd7ecd5454568262a4060e86d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95962bebe97a41a984eb0829e9dfdfa2",
      "statement": "The gateway integration keeps its credential boundary in Secrets Manager and call-time environment reads: `_gateway_client_secret()` resolves the client secret from `AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_CLIENT_SECRET_ARN`, `_gateway_token()` uses `AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_CLIENT_ID`, `AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_OAUTH_SCOPES`, and `AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_TOKEN_ENDPOINT`, and both functions read configuration inside the call rather than at import time to avoid binding stale test or runtime values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://fionaa/app/fionaa/gateway.py#L20-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d456869086eceee2d5ba4c6125b8eb10f7edf9c632f7f170af7a05fa35c8fda:"
        },
